		<chapter num="51">
			<heading>
				Psalm 51
			</heading>
			<heading>
				Create in Me a Clean Heart, O God
			</heading>
			<heading>
				To the choirmaster. A Psalm of David, when Nathan the prophet went to him, after he had gone in to Bathsheba.
			</heading>
			<begin-paragraph>
			</begin-paragraph>
			<v n="1">blot out my transgressions.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051002">
			</marker>
			<v n="2">cleanse me from my sin!</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051003">
			</marker>
			<v n="3">and my sin is ever before me.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051004">
			</marker>
			<v n="4">and blameless in your judgment.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051005">
			</marker>
			<v n="5">and in sin did my mother conceive me.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051006">
			</marker>
			<v n="6">and you teach me wisdom in the secret heart.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051007">
			</marker>
			<v n="7">whiter than snow.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051008">
			</marker>
			<v n="8">that you have broken rejoice.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051009">
			</marker>
			<v n="9">blot out all my iniquities.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051010">
			</marker>
			<v n="10">renew a right spirit within me.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051011">
			</marker>
			<v n="11">your Holy Spirit from me.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051012">
			</marker>
			<v n="12">and uphold me with a willing spirit.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051013">
			</marker>
			<v n="13">return to you.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051014">
			</marker>
			<v n="14">righteousness.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051015">
			</marker>
			<v n="15">and my mouth will declare your praise.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051016">
			</marker>
			<v n="16">you will not be pleased with a burnt offering.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051017">
			</marker>
			<v n="17">a broken and contrite heart, O God, you will not despise.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051018">
			</marker>
			<v n="18">build up the walls of Jerusalem;</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051019">
			</marker>
			<v n="19">then bulls will be offered on your altar.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19051020">
			</marker>
			<end-paragraph>
			</end-paragraph>
